+# Future-You Resume Lab
+
+## Concept
+
+A guided resume workshop transforms one vague bullet into credible evidence of next-level impact. The viewer moves through a four-part lens, an AI-assisted before-and-after, an accuracy check, three career-path filters, and a final LinkedIn visibility step.
+
+## Visual system
+
+- A paper-white resume canvas sits inside a navy workshop environment.
+- Gold marks decisions and outcomes; blue marks actions and editable fields.
+- The four-part lens is a recurring R-A-O-S rail: Responsibility, Action, Outcome, Scope.
+- Before/after copy is presented as designed resume fragments, not software screenshots.
+- Career-path scenes use three distinct routes: promotion, lateral move, and role redesign.
+
+## Motion approach
+
+One paused GSAP timeline drives all motion. Each narration beat is a timed clip with a unique ID. Cards, rules, and text enter with short, settled moves; no motion repeats infinitely. The final beat resolves by turning an ordinary headline into a future-facing signal.
+
+## Accessibility
+
+All important ideas appear as large, high-contrast type. Narration is preserved verbatim in the source. Decorative elements are marked as such, and meaning never depends on color alone.
